WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.289 --> 00:00:15.317
"Are you sure the threatening comment is gone?"

2
00:00:15.578 --> 00:00:16.418
Maggie asked.

3
00:00:17.419 --> 00:00:18.480
"It's no big deal, kids."

4
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.221
Jackson sounded distracted.

5
00:00:20.241 --> 00:00:22.342
"Maybe the mayor deleted it."

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:24.224
He pulled out his notebook.

7
00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:29.087
"I think I'll talk to the police and see if they found anything suspicious in Mrs.

8
00:00:29.127 --> 00:00:29.748
Sweet's shed.

9
00:00:30.668 --> 00:00:32.550
You kids should go home and work on your float."

10
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.673
"Are you sure you don't want any help?"

11
00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:36.674
Henry asked.

12
00:00:36.694 --> 00:00:40.778
"The Lemonade Detectives have solved lots of mysteries."

13
00:00:41.738 --> 00:00:42.699
Jackson smiled.

14
00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:43.860
"I know, Henry.

15
00:00:44.481 --> 00:00:45.122
But don't worry.

16
00:00:45.522 --> 00:00:48.225
If there's really a mystery here, I'll get to the bottom of it."

17
00:00:51.828 --> 00:00:53.670
He rushed off, whistling cheerfully.

18
00:00:54.691 --> 00:00:55.892
Henry glanced at Maggie.

19
00:00:56.796 --> 00:01:00.937
"Should we follow him and try to talk him into letting us hear what the police say?"

20
00:01:00.957 --> 00:01:04.618
"No, Jackson is right," Maggie said.

21
00:01:04.638 --> 00:01:08.359
"We need to finish our float, or we'll never win those prizes."

22
00:01:08.379 --> 00:01:10.400
"I guess you're right."

23
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.520
Henry smiled.

24
00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:17.022
"Maybe I just miss solving mysteries so much that I was hoping we'd found another one!"

25
00:01:18.042 --> 00:01:18.862
Maggie shrugged.

26
00:01:19.102 --> 00:01:19.642
"Not me.

27
00:01:20.302 --> 00:01:22.583
Nobody is offering to pay our detective fee.

28
00:01:23.463 --> 00:01:25.644
That means we don't have time to investigate."

29
00:01:26.572 --> 00:01:28.414
The two of them headed out of the auto shop.

30
00:01:29.395 --> 00:01:32.838
Right outside Henry spotted Snake leaning against a lamppost.

31
00:01:34.679 --> 00:01:36.221
"Hi, Snake," Henry said.

32
00:01:36.241 --> 00:01:39.484
"Is your band's float ready for the parade tomorrow?"

33
00:01:39.504 --> 00:01:41.646
"Hi, Lemonade Kids."

34
00:01:42.426 --> 00:01:43.287
Snake sighed.

35
00:01:43.828 --> 00:01:45.429
"We're not doing a float after all."

36
00:01:45.449 --> 00:01:47.931
"Really? What happened?"

37
00:01:48.272 --> 00:01:48.992
Maggie asked.

38
00:01:49.012 --> 00:01:52.776
"Our practice was going great yesterday," Snake said.

39
00:01:53.928 --> 00:01:56.670
"We were all having so much fun that we forgot about the time.

40
00:01:57.691 --> 00:02:00.112
One member of the band got grounded for coming home late."

41
00:02:01.233 --> 00:02:03.874
"Wow, that's too bad," Henry said.

42
00:02:03.894 --> 00:02:07.516
"So the whole band is dropping out of the parade?"

43
00:02:08.457 --> 00:02:09.658
"We don't have much choice."

44
00:02:10.038 --> 00:02:10.798
Snake shrugged.

45
00:02:10.818 --> 00:02:14.301
"Our music wouldn't sound right without all of us playing."

46
00:02:15.341 --> 00:02:18.483
"Oh. Well sorry," Henry said.

47
00:02:19.043 --> 00:02:19.684
"See you around."

48
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.320
He and Maggie wandered off.

49
00:02:25.401 --> 00:02:28.202
Maggie glanced back to make sure Snake was out of earshot.

50
00:02:28.222 --> 00:02:31.602
"Snake looked pretty upset," she said.

51
00:02:31.622 --> 00:02:33.463
"But this is good news for us.

52
00:02:34.443 --> 00:02:36.884
It means we'll have less competition for those prizes!"

53
00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.545
Henry nodded, but he wasn't really listening.

54
00:02:41.765 --> 00:02:44.106
He'd just noticed the town hall building up ahead.

55
00:02:44.126 --> 00:02:50.708
"Jackson said Mayor Porter might have deleted that threatening comment from the website," he said.

56
00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.602
"Maybe we should stop in and ask the mayor if that's true."

57
00:02:55.622 --> 00:02:56.703
Maggie looked uncertain.

58
00:02:56.723 --> 00:02:59.424
"Do you still think there's a mystery going on?"

59
00:02:59.444 --> 00:03:02.226
"I don't know," Henry said.

60
00:03:02.246 --> 00:03:07.029
"It's possible that the threatening comment was a joke, and Mrs.

61
00:03:07.089 --> 00:03:09.150
Sweet just misplaced her candy.

62
00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:14.433
But it's also possible that someone is trying to ruin the parade."

63
00:03:14.453 --> 00:03:16.974
"Okay," Maggie said.

64
00:03:16.994 --> 00:03:18.235
"But let's hurry.

65
00:03:18.655 --> 00:03:20.236
I want to get back to our float soon."

66
00:03:23.392 --> 00:03:24.993
They went into the town hall building.

67
00:03:28.054 --> 00:03:30.895
The mayor's secretary was a cheerful young man named Mr.

68
00:03:30.935 --> 00:03:36.558
Beck. "I'm sorry, kids," he said after Henry and Maggie asked to see the mayor.

69
00:03:36.578 --> 00:03:39.919
"Mayor Porter has meetings all afternoon.

70
00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:43.160
I can make an appointment for you on Monday, if you like."

71
00:03:44.301 --> 00:03:46.122
"Monday's too late," Maggie said.

72
00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:48.383
"It's about the parade tomorrow."

73
00:03:49.363 --> 00:03:50.083
Henry nodded.

74
00:03:50.103 --> 00:03:51.644
"It might be important."

75
00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:53.192
"Might be?"

76
00:03:53.472 --> 00:03:54.513
Mr. Beck echoed.

77
00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:55.793
"What do you mean?"

78
00:03:55.813 --> 00:04:01.416
"We're afraid someone might be trying to sabotage the parade," Henry said.

79
00:04:01.436 --> 00:04:05.478
"Mrs. Sweet thinks someone broke into her shed last night.

80
00:04:06.558 --> 00:04:10.180
And there was a threatening message in the comments on the town website."

81
00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.720
"Oh dear.

82
00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.421
Really?" Mr.

83
00:04:13.461 --> 00:04:15.962
Beck quickly opened the town website on his computer.

84
00:04:15.982 --> 00:04:20.424
"I didn't notice anything like that when I was updating the site a few minutes ago."

85
00:04:21.536 --> 00:04:23.318
"You mean you didn't delete the comment?"

86
00:04:23.658 --> 00:04:24.438
Maggie asked.

87
00:04:24.458 --> 00:04:27.601
"Only the person who leaves the comment can delete it."

88
00:04:27.881 --> 00:04:29.603
Mr. Beck sounded skeptical now.

89
00:04:29.623 --> 00:04:31.124
"What did you kids see?"

90
00:04:31.144 --> 00:04:36.708
"There was a message right after the one by Miss Bishop," Henry explained.

91
00:04:36.728 --> 00:04:42.173
"It said the parade was for losers, and the mayor should cancel it, or else."

92
00:04:43.594 --> 00:04:45.916
"Hmm." A second later Mr.

93
00:04:45.956 --> 00:04:47.757
Beck closed the town website page.

94
00:04:47.777 --> 00:04:51.140
"Well, I'll mention the comment to the mayor when I see him."

95
00:04:52.128 --> 00:04:55.209
Henry could tell the secretary wasn't taking this seriously.

96
00:04:55.229 --> 00:04:57.890
"But what if—," he began.

97
00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.550
"This is an outrage!"

98
00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.431
an angry shout interrupted him.

99
00:05:02.571 --> 00:05:05.792
An older, white-haired man had just stomped into the office.

100
00:05:06.953 --> 00:05:09.473
He looked familiar, but Henry didn't know his name.

101
00:05:09.493 --> 00:05:11.114
"Good afternoon, Mr.

102
00:05:11.134 --> 00:05:11.954
Fleming," Mr.

103
00:05:11.974 --> 00:05:13.195
Beck greeted the older man.

104
00:05:13.215 --> 00:05:14.735
"Is something wrong?"

105
00:05:15.695 --> 00:05:17.596
"You bet your life something's wrong!"

106
00:05:18.728 --> 00:05:22.451
Mr. Fleming pushed past Henry and Maggie and glared at the secretary.

107
00:05:22.471 --> 00:05:26.274
"The window of my art studio overlooks an empty lot.

108
00:05:27.395 --> 00:05:29.257
I like it that way—very quiet.

109
00:05:30.138 --> 00:05:33.481
But this week the high school soccer team has been building a float there.

110
00:05:34.421 --> 00:05:38.565
So there's been hammering, sawing, shouting, and laughing all day long.

111
00:05:39.646 --> 00:05:40.787
I can't take it anymore!

112
00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:46.031
If someone doesn't do something, I'll sue the town to call off the parade!"
